<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Ms. Earhart returns two weeks after her first visit, on the day of her otolaryngology appointment, and is seen the same day by Dr. Lindgren. She has rinsed with saline twice daily and used fluticasone every morning since the first visit, and has not used a decongestant spray or the nighttime cold tablet. Five days ago the left side became worse again: the drainage turned thick and yellow-green, the pressure over the left cheek and forehead increased, and her left upper teeth ache. She has felt warm, and her temperature today is 37.6 °C. Her eosinophil count and total IgE from the first visit were normal. She has not flown since the first visit. SNOT-22 today 58, from 52. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Treatment</td><td>Saline irrigation twice daily and fluticasone daily for two weeks</td></tr><tr><td>Flare</td><td>Five days of thicker discolored drainage, more left facial pressure, aching left upper teeth</td></tr><tr><td>Scores</td><td>SNOT-22 58; facial pain 7 of 10</td></tr><tr><td>First-visit results</td><td>Eosinophils 0.21 x10^3/uL; total IgE 42 IU/mL</td></tr><tr><td>Flying</td><td>Grounded herself since the first visit</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

